&lt;p&gt;If these values resonate with you and our vision excites you, join us today and help us end cyber attacks from the endpoint to everywhere! #Defenders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don’t meet every single requirement?&amp;nbsp;Studies have shown that women and people of color are less likely to apply to jobs unless they meet every single qualification. At Cybereason we are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace (#uBu), so if you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About Us:&lt;br&gt;Join us at Cybereason, where we&#39;re pioneering groundbreaking cybersecurity solutions to protect organizations&lt;br&gt;worldwide. At the forefront of endpoint security, our advanced technology and research-driven team are creating a&lt;br&gt;safer digital environment. We are seeking a dynamic Project Manager who is passionate about driving projects that&lt;br&gt;merge cutting-edge technology and strategic innovation.&lt;br&gt;The Role:&lt;br&gt;As a Project Manager, you will lead complex projects from conception to completion, managing timelines, resources,&lt;br&gt;and stakeholder engagement. You&#39;ll work closely with cross-functional teams to ensure our project deliverables align&lt;br&gt;with strategic objectives and exceed industry standards.&lt;br&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;br&gt;● Develop and manage a detailed project schedule and work plan&lt;br&gt;● Provide project updates on a consistent basis to various stakeholders about strategy, adjustments, and&lt;br&gt;progress&lt;br&gt;● Utilize industry best practices, techniques, and standards throughout entire project execution&lt;br&gt;● Monitor and measure project performance to identify areas for improvement&lt;br&gt;● Manage contracts with vendors and suppliers by assigning tasks and communicating expected deliverables&lt;br&gt;Requirements:&lt;br&gt;● Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, business, or a related field&lt;br&gt;● 5+ years of project management&lt;br&gt;● 3+ years of experience with Jira and Salesforce&lt;br&gt;● 2+ years working background in cybersecurity (from private or public sectors)&lt;br&gt;● Fluent English and at least intermediate Japanese (JLPT is not required, but the level should be N2 or higher)&lt;br&gt;● Proven ability to solve problems creatively&lt;br&gt;● Strong familiarity with project management software tools, methodologies, and best practices&lt;br&gt;● Experience seeing projects through the full lifecycle&lt;br&gt;● Excellent analytical skills&lt;br&gt;● Strong interpersonal skills and extremely resourceful&lt;br&gt;● Proven ability to complete projects according to outlined scope, budget, and timeline&lt;br&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;● Good understanding of endpoint security or previous work experience with endpoint security products&lt;br&gt;● Basic understanding of ransomware, malware, and desktop risks&lt;br&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;● Competitive salary and compensation structure&lt;br&gt;● Dynamic and inclusive work environment&lt;br&gt;● Opportunities for professional growth and advancement&lt;br&gt;● Cutting-edge technology and tools&lt;br&gt;● Flexible working hours with a hybrid office model&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More About Cybereason:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
